  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_1",
      "quote": "We considered studies of any design as long as they had a comparison group that investigated VE against SARS-CoV-2 infection and/or asymptomatic SARS-CoV-2 infection after vaccination with an EMA-approved COVID-19 vaccine (see Supplement Part S2 for complete population intervention comparison outcomes (PICO) questions).",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies key eligibility components (population, intervention, outcomes, requirement for a comparison group, restriction to EMA-approved vaccines) and refers to a PICO in the supplement; it does not explicitly list all study characteristics (e.g. settings, specific follow-up requirements) within the provided evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_1",
      "quote": "No restrictions were made regarding publication language or status. The review started on 1 January 2021. The end date of this interim analysis was 14 May 2021.",
      "reason": "The report explicitly states language and publication-status eligibility (no restrictions) and gives the review start and end dates, addressing dissemination timing."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No explicit distinction is provided in the retrieved evidence between excluding studies because outcomes were not measured versus excluding because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "table_0",
      "quote": "| Study population (n)                           | General population (cases: n = 35,979; controls: n = 35,979) | HCW (n = 9,109) | ... | Study design                                   | Case-control study (test-negative design) | Retrospective cohort study | ... | Vaccine                                        | Comirnaty | Comirnaty | ...",
      "reason": "The manuscript and tables present and distinguish groups used in analyses (e.g. vaccinated vs unvaccinated, vaccine types, dose 1 vs dose 2, populations such as HCW or LTCF), but there is no clear, explicit statement linking each synthesis grouping to the specific comparisons defined in the review objectives in the provided evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_1",
      "quote": "We considered studies of any design as long as they had a comparison group that investigated VE against SARS-CoV-2 infection and/or asymptomatic SARS-CoV-2 infection after vaccination with an EMA-approved COVID-19 vaccine ... Vaccination against severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection plays a key role in the containment of the coronavirus disease (COVID19) pandemic. All vaccines approved by the European Medical Agency (EMA) at the time of writing demonstrated high vaccine efficacy/effectiveness (VE) against severe COVID-19. With vaccination programmes being implemented in most European countries, it becomes urgent to assess the extent to which these vaccines are also able to prevent symptomatic and asymptomatic infections to guide public health recommendations and develop strategies for fully vaccinated people.",
      "reason": "The report restricts eligibility to EMA-approved vaccines and provides a rationale (focus on EMA-approved vaccines because of their relevance for public health recommendations and the need to assess their effectiveness)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 75
}

